<title>USA: N.Y. business loans fell $649 mln in June 25 week.</title>
<headline>N.Y. business loans fell $649 mln in June 25 week.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commercial and industrial loans at the six major New York banks, excluding acceptances, fell $649 million to $45,599 million in the week ended June 25, the Federal Reserve Bank of New York said.</p>
<p>Including acceptances, loans fell $644 million to $45,870 million.</p>
<p>Commercial paper outstanding nationally fell $2.527 billion to $871,901 billion.</p>
<p>(( -- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660 ))</p>
